  "faq_h2": "Y2K symbols, answered",
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What are Y2K symbols?",
      "a": "Y2K symbols are Unicode characters that capture the early-2000s cyber aesthetic: sparkle stars (✦ ✮ ⋆), gothic crosses (♱ ✟ †), butterflies (🦋), CDs and pagers (💿 📟), and frosted dust marks. Because they are plain Unicode rather than images, you can copy and paste them straight into any bio, username, or caption without uploading a file."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I use Y2K symbols in an Instagram bio?",
      "a": "Tap any symbol or combo on this page to copy it, then open Instagram, go to Edit Profile, and paste it into your name or bio field. Frame your text with matching symbols, for example ♱ your text ♱ or 𓆩♡𓆪, and add a sparkle (✦) or star (✮) between words. Keep it to two or three symbols so the bio stays readable."
    },
    {
      "q": "Do Y2K symbols work on TikTok and Discord?",
      "a": "Yes. Every symbol here is standard Unicode, so it renders in TikTok display names, bios, captions, and comments, and in Discord display names, channel names, and messages. TikTok and Discord usernames (the @handle) accept only letters, numbers, periods and underscores, so keep the symbols in the display name. A few rare glyphs may show as a box on older devices that lack the font, so preview on your phone before posting. Plain stars, hearts, and crosses have the widest support."
    }
  ],
